The EIGENSOFT package combines functionality from population genetics
methods (Patterson et al. 2006) and the EIGENSTRAT stratification
correction method (Price et al. 2006).

EIGENSTRAT uses principal components analysis (PCA) to explicitly model
ancestry differences between cases and controls along continuous axes of
variation; the resulting correction is specific to a candidate marker's
variation in frequency across ancestral populations, minimizing spurious
associations while maximizing power to detect true associations.
